cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite it and the field dataset it analyses as below."
type: software
title: "KelpObserve Sesimbra 2026: reproduction archive of the satellite kelp-cover benchmark, its revisions and the optics prerequisites"
version: "1.0.0"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23478585
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/KelpObserve/kelpobserve"
abstract: "Code, registrations, input locks and archived runs behind the Sesimbra kelp-cover technical report of the AQUASERV Transnational Access project KelpObserve (PID 42082): the registered benchmark of Sentinel-2 and Pléiades Neo against CCMAR diver quadrats, its exploratory revisions r1 to r6, and the E2c and E5s optics analyses. A replay command reruns each experiment in an isolated workspace and compares every output with the archived run."
authors:
  - family-names: "Rusu"
    given-names: "Andrei"
    affiliation: "Pine View Software AS (Pineview), Norway"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-1219-4816"
keywords:
  - "kelp"
  - "Saccorhiza polyschides"
  - "satellite remote sensing"
  - "Sentinel-2"
  - "Pléiades Neo"
  - "water-column correction"
  - "pre-registration"
  - "reproducibility"
  - "Sesimbra"
  - "AQUASERV"
  - "KelpObserve"
